  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Motors received $633M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. General Motors won 13,904 awards so far, with an average award size of $45.5K, and obligations are up 124.6% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show a pattern of fluctuation: FY21 was $187M, FY22 was $188M, FY23 was $260M, FY24 was $182M, FY25 was $282M, and FY26 to date is $633M. The FY26 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure; award-value figures in specific tables are total contract values rather than obligations. These figures show General Motors’ current federal presence in dollar terms, the number of awards driving that total, and how obligations changed across recent fiscal years. Use the award count and average award size to understand transaction scale, and use the fiscal year series to track year-to-year movement in obligations. The FY26 to date total dominates the recent series, reflecting the firm's current-year federal activity as recorded in the available figures.",
